[Jet]
You bring your elbows back and your head forward and make to get up; however, something stops you. An invisible something. A heavy something pinning you down. Whatever it is, it's like it's sitting on your stomach with all its weight.

[Narrator]
You can't escape. Your arms feel staticky. Your legs are jelly, hollow-boned.

[Jet]
"Maybe tomorrow", you think to yourself. But how many tomorrows has it been already?

[Jet]
Maybe...

[Jet]
Maybe I could just brush my teeth for today?

[Jet]
Yeah, yeah, that sounds doable.

[Narrator]
With a long and sharp exhalation of breath, control returns to your body slowly: first in your fingers and toes, then your thighs and arms, and finally the rest of you.